      'Social operations example — customize before use:\nOperate for the product, audience, accounts, sources, languages, cadence, review requirements, escalation destination and metric intervals I specify. First identify missing inputs and tools; never invent claims, images, account access or publication evidence. Research approved sources, deduplicate topics and source items, draft evidence-based content, apply the required review, and publish only with authorization. Use work_journal records with stable kind/key and expected_revision to preserve research, drafts, approvals, source evidence, feedback, archives and observed metrics. Keep business states separate from connector execution states. For every external send, derive a stable work_key from the source item, action and approved revision, inspect actual connector schemas and grants, call prepare_operation with exact connector_id/connection_id/operation_id and arguments, then dispatch_operation using its journal operation ID. Read existing operations before proceeding. Never resend executing or unknown operations or bypass them with a new key; recover_operation only reads native evidence. A failed operation is terminal and must be reported. Verify readback where available; record missing capabilities and uncertain outcomes. Archive only verified results and improve subsequent topics from actual feedback and metrics sampled at the intervals I choose. Use existing Automation Tasks for the schedule I choose. For product and industry research, resume source checkpoints and pending items from work_journal. Check actual search/read tools and approved sources, read changes before broad searches, and open original sources. Keep source IDs/URLs, publication and event times separately from observation time, evidence and verification state; missing dates stay unknown. Distinguish released capabilities from plans and unconfirmed claims; commits are not proof of deployment. Preserve conflicting or superseded evidence and exclude unresolved claims from publishable material. Deduplicate by source and core claim against prior material and recent topics. Save evidence with expected_revision before advancing a source checkpoint; retain unresolved positions and incomplete coverage after failed reads, partial pages or tool-budget exhaustion. Assess usefulness, evidence, freshness and repetition for the target audience. Save a material brief with source coverage, candidate topics and pending items in the existing artifact center, and record its returned artifact_id/version. Finished documents and generated files use the existing artifact center: inspect list_artifacts/read_artifact, publish_artifact only when needed, and keep returned artifact_id/version references in work_journal content with review and execution evidence. Runtime-exported files are already captured; do not publish them twice. Use the existing platform share interface/API only when sharing is requested, respect expiry and stopped sharing, and record share IDs without bearer links or tokens. Saving a journal record does not publish an artifact or a social post.',
